WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.918
The purpose of my program is to have a soccer ball move

2
00:00:02.918 --> 00:00:05.200
around the stage until my mouse catches it.

3
00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:09.105
When the green flag is clicked, the reset block resets

4
00:00:09.105 --> 00:00:09.890
the program.

5
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.070
Then the ball says booting up.

6
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.370
Next it says, try to stop me with your mouse.

7
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.596
My code works by using a conditional loop in this part

8
00:00:18.596 --> 00:00:21.250
to keep the ball moving until my mouse touches it.

9
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.979
Inside the loop, the first set block picks a random

10
00:00:24.979 --> 00:00:25.840
number for x.

11
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.640
The second set block picks a random number for y.

12
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.440
Then the glide block moves the ball to that new spot.

13
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.836
After every move, the repeat until block checks if my

14
00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:40.045
mouse is touching the ball. My mouse missed, so the loop

15
00:00:40.045 --> 00:00:42.680
runs again and the ball moves to another spot.

16
00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:46.131
This time my mouse lands on the ball, so the repeat

17
00:00:46.131 --> 00:00:49.110
until block stops the loop, and the program ends.

18
00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:52.366
Conditional loops are different than regular repeats. In

19
00:00:52.366 --> 00:00:54.899
my program I can't use a repeat and have to use a

20
00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:57.691
conditional repeat because I don't know how many times

21
00:00:57.691 --> 00:01:00.587
the ball will move before my mouse catches it. A regular

22
00:01:00.587 --> 00:01:03.431
repeat needs a set number, like ten. But my mouse could

23
00:01:03.431 --> 00:01:06.275
catch the ball after two moves, or after twenty. So the

24
00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:09.119
repeat until block keeps the ball moving until my mouse

25
00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:10.670
touches it, and then it stops.

